<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of</p>
<p>the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of</p>
<p>25 billion escudos of five-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23 Mar 2002</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED: 25 bln esc     COUPON: 5.75 pct</p>
<p>    AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.4955</p>
<p>    HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 5.5 LOWEST: 5.48</p>
<p>    BIDS: 66.55 bln esc PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Annual</p>
<p>    PAYMENT DATE: 29 Jul 1997</p>
<p>    NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 239.20 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
